{%- comment -%}
  Display-style section heading, matching the NH ONE design spec
  (.claude/resources/design_theme.jpeg): title case, two-tone — the heading
  colour, with the accented part in the brand colour — and no underline.

  MARKING THE BRAND-COLOURED PART
  Put a pipe immediately before it in the heading text. Everything after the
  pipe is brand-coloured; everything before it uses the heading colour:

      "SHOP BY |CATEGORY"      ->  Shop by <brand>Category</brand>
      "SHOP BY |CAR BRAND"     ->  Shop by <brand>Car Brand</brand>
      "LATEST FROM |OUR BLOGS" ->  Latest from <brand>Our Blogs</brand>

  The accent can be several words, and spaces around the pipe are optional.
  A heading with no pipe simply renders entirely in the heading colour.

  Merchants type these headings in caps in the theme editor, so the text is
  down-cased and re-capitalised word by word here. Short connector words stay
  lowercase — "Shop by Category", not "Shop By Category" — unless they open the
  heading or the accented part.

  Accepts:
  - heading {String} - raw heading text from the section settings.

  Usage:
  {% render 'section-heading', heading: section.settings.title %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Whitespace normalisation, and it is load-bearing. Headings pasted into the
  theme editor routinely contain NON-BREAKING spaces (U+00A0) and runs of two
  or more spaces — this store has both ("FEATURED<U+00A0>PRODUCTS",
  "TOP-SELLING<U+00A0><U+00A0>PRODUCTS"). Liquid's `split: ' '` matches neither,
  so without this the whole heading comes back as a single word.

  The first `replace` below takes a LITERAL U+00A0. It looks like an ordinary
  space in an editor — do not "tidy" it into one, or word splitting silently
  breaks again. The second pads the pipe so it survives as its own token
  whether the merchant wrote "BY |CATEGORY" or "BY|CATEGORY". The loop then
  drops the empty tokens left behind by repeated spaces.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign normalised_heading = heading | replace: ' ', ' ' | replace: '|', ' | ' | strip -%}
{%- assign raw_words = normalised_heading | split: ' ' -%}

{%- assign lead_words = '' -%}
{%- assign accent_words = '' -%}
{%- assign in_accent = false -%}

{%- for raw_word in raw_words -%}
  {%- unless raw_word == blank -%}
    {%- if raw_word == '|' -%}
      {%- assign in_accent = true -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign lower_word = raw_word | downcase -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        A connector keeps its lowercase form, except when it is the first word
        of the heading or the first word of the accented part.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        `assign` cannot hold a comparison in Liquid — `assign x = a == b` is a
        syntax error — so the boolean is set through an if/else.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign starts_part = false -%}
      {%- if in_accent -%}
        {%- if accent_words == blank -%}
          {%- assign starts_part = true -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- if lead_words == blank -%}
          {%- assign starts_part = true -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- assign is_connector = false -%}
      {%- unless starts_part -%}
        {%- case lower_word -%}
          {%- when 'by', 'of', 'and', 'the', 'for', 'to', 'in', 'a', 'on', 'with', 'from' -%}
            {%- assign is_connector = true -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
      {%- endunless -%}

      {%- if is_connector -%}
        {%- assign display_word = lower_word -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign display_word = lower_word | capitalize -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if in_accent -%}
        {%- assign accent_words = accent_words | append: display_word | append: ' ' -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign lead_words = lead_words | append: display_word | append: ' ' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if lead_words != blank or accent_words != blank -%}
  <h2 class="section-heading section-heading--display">
    {{- lead_words -}}
    {%- if accent_words != blank -%}
      <span class="section-heading__accent">{{ accent_words | strip }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </h2>
{%- endif -%}
